/-!
# B3 (chunk kernel), part 8: the chunk kernel in IL

`chunkI pM`: with the chunk table `tabK …` on `dT` and the row `x` (length `λ`) on stack `0`, it
replaces `x` by `chunkG2 … x` and leaves the table in place; all its other stacks end empty.

The table (`tabK`): the header `[λ, 2^P, 2^(P+1), nb, |tab|, 2^pk, 2^b, 2(λ - Σn)]`, the four
stage tables reversed, then per block `blkHdr n pk b ++ am ++ ap`.
